# Fixed 2026-11-27, defect 2876, lane runtime-names: the switch the
# runtime's `heroes_unit.h` defines, bound through a header of the program's
# own that takes it back and defines it again as `7`.
# Symptom: told as a name `heroes_runtime.h` declares, whose functions free
# what the program holds.
# Cause and repair: `fixedbugs-2876-the-switch-heroes-unit-h-defines-bound-through-it-is-told-as-its-macro`.
# Still the runtime's: the unit defines it before the program's header, and
# a binding of it reads what the compiler set unless a header undoes the
# compiler's switch, as this one does (measured: `7` here, `1` under a
# header that defines nothing).

extern "fixedbugs-2876-defines-the-switch-again.h"
    constant HERO_STANDARD_AFTER_GROUPS: i64  #~ ffi_runtime_header

function main()
    print(HERO_STANDARD_AFTER_GROUPS)
